WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:05.493
You placed each setting in its control
plane: Intune for endpoint policy,

3
00:00:05.493 --> 00:00:10.187
the Defender portal for what Intune
doesn't hold, and one plane per setting.

4
00:00:10.187 --> 00:00:14.201
You checked what your government cloud
offers, and how to record what it doesn't.

5
00:00:14.201 --> 00:00:18.338
You read incidents through Microsoft
Graph, in the tenant's own cloud.

6
00:00:18.338 --> 00:00:21.949
And you proved the sensor, on
one device and across the fleet.

7
00:00:21.949 --> 00:00:24.759
The evidence an I S S O
keeps from this module:

8
00:00:24.759 --> 00:00:27.724
the role export and the
pim assignment report,

9
00:00:27.724 --> 00:00:32.093
the E D R policy export and its
assignments, the weekly coverage file,

10
00:00:32.093 --> 00:00:34.902
the detection test with
the alert it raised,

11
00:00:34.902 --> 00:00:38.725
and the exception register for
every device not onboarded.

12
00:00:38.725 --> 00:00:42.807
Next is Module 2, prevention
and Attack Surface Reduction,

13
00:00:42.807 --> 00:00:47.450
where the settings move through
audit, warn and block, ring by ring.
